If you supply me with some nouns, adjectives, and adverbs, I
will use them to tell you a story that you might find amusing.
First, tell me the name of a man that you know pretty well.
Just the first name will do.
$ Ishmael
Think of some nouns (names of things).
I need four of them, so enter the first.
$ harpoon
Now a second one,
$ whale
and a third,
$ boat
and one more.
$ island
I also need the name of a place.
$ Tahiti
Now enter a plural noun.
$ fishes
Now think of adjectives (that describe something or somebody).
I need four of those.
Just press RETURN after each one.
$ salty
$ windy
$ rigorous
$ satirical
Now for some adverbs (that tells how something is done; it will
usually end in "ly").  I need two.
$ pottentiously
$ allegorically
Thank you.

When you are ready to appreciate the story you have helped
write, press the RETURN key.
$ 
[H[2J                When Ishmael Got Most Excited

   Ishmael left work on Friday night after a salty week and started
to drive to Tahiti.  His car was acting windy but it was running
pottentiously.  There were lots of fishes in the car with him so no 
wonder he was rigorous.  Events went from bad to worse as he saw a 
harpoon in the street and ran his whale into it.  A satirical lady tried 
to hit him with her boat and he allegorically escaped.  He had no more 
island by the time he reached home.
   Well, that's all I heard about it.
